<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- §3.7 / nfc_contact_exchange: contact exchange via NDEF tag-in-tag
	     writes (see `lib/core/contact/nfc_android.dart`, `Ndef.write`).
	     No FeliCa/ISO7816/ISO15693/MiFare use anywhere in `lib/` — NDEF is
	     the only format the app reads or writes, so it is the only one
	     requested here. Required by the `nfc_manager` plugin's own iOS
	     setup instructions (pub.dev, "Near Field Communication Tag Reader
	     Session Formats Entitlement"); without it, `NfcManager.instance
	     .startSession` fails at the OS level regardless of
	     NFCReaderUsageDescription (Info.plist:73), which only covers the
	     usage-description dialog, not the capability itself.

	     Requires the "Near Field Communication Tag Reading" capability to
	     be enabled for this App ID in the Apple Developer portal, and the
	     "Cleona Distribution" provisioning profile regenerated afterwards
	     — otherwise codesign fails ("profile doesn't support this
	     capability") on the very next Manual-signed build (CODE_SIGN_STYLE
	     = Manual, project.pbxproj). UNGEPRUEFT: no Apple device or Xcode
	     available in this session to confirm the profile already carries
	     it. -->
	<!-- S397 (25.09.2026): TAG, not NDEF. nfc_manager 3.5.1 opens an
	     NFCTagReaderSession (ios/Classes/SwiftNfcManagerPlugin.swift:92),
	     whose format is TAG; NDEF belongs to NFCNDEFReaderSession, which the
	     plugin does not use. App Store Connect rejected the upload of
	     v4.2.0-beta: "entitlement 'com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats'
	     ... 'NDEF is disallowed'. (90778)" (SDK 26.5, min OS 15.5). NDEF tags
	     are still read and written through the TAG session. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.nfc.readersession.formats</key>
	<array>
		<string>TAG</string>
	</array>

	<!-- §7.2 / mycelium neighbour search: the app joins the multicast
	     group 239.192.67.76 on call port 41341 at node start
	     (`mycelium/lib/neighbours.dart:83`, the join itself at
	     `mycelium/lib/neighbours_channel.dart:70`, opened from
	     `mycelium/lib/node_call.dart:63` — iOS runs the same in-process
	     node as every platform). Without this entitlement iOS refuses
	     the join at the socket level; `neighbours_listener.dart` catches
	     that and the search degrades to broadcast-only (§7.2: fall back
	     to the wildcard address and continue — not an error), so a
	     missing grant costs segment-wide group discovery, not the app.

	     The same entitlement covers the other group joins: the CalDAV
	     auto-discovery joins mDNS 224.0.0.251 to receive answers for
	     its `_caldav._tcp` / `_caldavs._tcp` queries
	     (`lib/core/calendar/sync/caldav_discovery.dart:58`; without the
	     grant it returns empty, caught and logged). Dormant:
	     `lib/core/calls/lan_multicast.dart:64` joins ff02::c1e0:ca11
	     for group-call media, but its only path,
	     `MediaRelay.onSendMulticast`
	     (`lib/core/calls/group_call_manager.dart:690`), currently
	     falls back to unicast per child — the day it is wired it needs
	     this entitlement too.

	     RESTRICTED entitlement: granted by Apple per request (portal,
	     "Multicast Networking" additional capability, team 3YQ8UFCFU7).
	     History: removed 25.09.2026 (owner decision C) because the
	     release profile did not carry the capability, granted by Apple
	     on 03.10.2026 and put back. NOT added to
	     `macos/Runner/*.entitlements`: macOS does not consult this
	     entitlement (Apple DTS), and the macOS app runs outside the
	     sandbox (macos/Runner/Release.entitlements). The RELEASE gate in
	     `.github/workflows/ios-build.yml` ("Install provisioning
	     profile") fails the job when a key of this file is missing from
	     the profile — the unsigned VERIFY build cannot see that. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.networking.multicast</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
